WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.237
This work is entirely theoretical: no datasets,
benchmarks, or experiments,

00:00:05.317 --> 00:00:06.726
only proven theorems.

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:11.830
The losses are non-negative and differentiable with
Lipschitz gradients,

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:16.580
but possibly non-convex, like sine-squared and
quartic polynomials.
